<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Marwanids</h1><p class="st-meta">990 CE – 1085 CE (approx.) · capital Mayyafariqin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kurdish dynasty that ruled Diyar Bakr from Mayyafariqin and Amid, with a long, prosperous reign under Nasr al-Dawla in the 11th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the 980s the Kurdish chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badh">Badh</a> took advantage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyid</a> weakness to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a>, Amid and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyar-bakr">Diyar Bakr</a>. After his death in 990 his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-ali-al-hasan-ibn-marwan">Abu Ali ibn Marwan</a> took over the domain, founding the dynasty that bears his father's name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasr-al-dawla-ibn-marwan">Nasr al-Dawla Ahmad ibn Marwan</a> ruled for about fifty years (1011-1061), keeping peace with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> by diplomacy and gifts. His capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a> gained mosques, a hospital and bridges, and attracted scholars, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-dawla-ibn-jahir">Ibn Jahir</a> and refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. The population mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurds">Kurds</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac-christians">Syriac Christians</a>, and the dynasty was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasr-al-dawla-ibn-marwan">Nasr al-Dawla</a>'s death the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. Around 1085 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik-Shah</a> sent its former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-dawla-ibn-jahir">Fakhr al-Dawla ibn Jahir</a> to conquer it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyar-bakr">Diyar Bakr</a> passed to Seljuk governors and later to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/inalids">Inalids</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/artuqids-of-mardin">Artuqids</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 990 CE – 1085 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.40%;width:1.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>990 CE – 1085 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mayyafariqin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Badh, Nasr al-Dawla Ahmad, Nizam al-Din Nasr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kurdish, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marwanid dynasty, Dostkis, Marwanids, Marwanid emirate of Diyar Bakr</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1038&amp;focus=marwanids" aria-label="Marwanids on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5701 807 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Marwanids lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6021 1063L6134 1224M6021 1063L6481 1127"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0M6481 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6021 1063h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6021 1063h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mayyafariqin. <a href="/atlas?year=1038&amp;focus=marwanids">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

